.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets — config.load_project_env reads .env from the project root; it must
# never be committable. Example files without values stay tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime state (never part of the immutable code root) — governed by
# core.paths (ANTIGONA_STATE_ROOT) and excluded from the production manifest.
.memory/
.tasks/
.task_messages/
.context/
.voice_cache/
.voice_settings.json
.health/
.logs/
workspace/
downloads/
antigona.db
antigona_sessions.db
antigona_memory.db
audit.db
audit_log.db
cli_state.json
cli_state.json.tmp
elevation.db
traces.db
traces.jsonl
mcp_servers.json
owner_pin.json
cli_aliases.json
cli_theme.json
cli_user_themes.json
legacy_reachability.jsonl

# Runtime state written into the code root when ANTIGONA_STATE_ROOT is unset.
# Measured 2026-09-17 on a real published clone: one gateway run left these
# untracked inside the code root, while antigona_sessions.db (line 24) and
# .memory/ (line 13) were already ignored. Dev defaults resolve to the code root
# via core.paths (project_local_dir() = project_root()/".antigona", lines 85-87;
# sandbox_isolation.json line 330, provider_state.json line 340). Only these
# untracked runtime files are ignored. .antigona/gateway_config.json is
# deliberately NOT listed: it is tracked in the index, and git never applies
# ignore rules to tracked files, so an ignore entry for it would protect nothing
# while falsely implying the tracked file could be dropped (regression-guarded
# by tests/unit/test_gitignore_tracked_paths.py). Tracked .antigona/ content
# (e.g. .antigona/personalities/*.md) stays tracked.
antigona_sessions.db-wal
antigona_sessions.db-shm
.antigona/sandbox_isolation.json
.antigona/provider_state.json
